  "checked_findings": [
    "Cached mapped class files contain a direct virtual Mob finalizeSpawn reference, an add-with-passengers reference, the Forge pack size call and group-stop reference in their class linkage. The cited source records their method-level order; the class-level references alone do not prove individual instruction offsets.",
    "Packaged Forge coremods register a method redirector. It targets NaturalSpawner and the Ocean Monument piece, matches a mapped virtual finalizeSpawn descriptor and replaces that call with ForgeEventFactory.onFinalizeSpawn. This establishes the available transform, with no transformed running-class claim.",
    "The helper posts FinalizeSpawn before forwarding the event values. Event cancellation skips subtype initialization and returns null group data, while leaving the independent spawn admission decision. The candidate tropical fish appearance propagation and rare inner-loop break therefore describe default, unchanged initialization only.",
    "setSpawnCancelled instead marks Mob; ForgeInternalHandler cancels its fresh EntityJoinLevelEvent at HIGHEST on the ServerLevel admission route. WorldGenRegion has a separate direct spawn-cancel guard. A join callback precedes insertion and UUID uniqueness, and absence of a callback cannot by itself distinguish all vetoes."
  ],
