    "identity_gap": "Driver and passive observer carry the NATURAL candidate across callbacks by UUID alone. A canceled join may return before removal from the candidate set. If a later different object with the same UUID is offered in the same bounded session, the stale provenance could be misassociated. This is a source scenario, not a historical event claim.",
    "alive_gap": "Driver later uses identical registry object and !isRemoved. LivingEntity.isAlive additionally requires health > 0. A present but dying instance could satisfy the current predicate before removal. The retained historical acceptance totals were not recalculated.",
    "minimal_future_qa_fix": "Keep identity of exact Mob, ServerLevel, NATURAL finalize attempt and bounded tick scope together up to actual fresh admission, expire unused candidates or close them when the original add returns, and verify same object isAlive() at a later server tick. Keep canceled initialization, denied admission and positive later presence distinct. No observer result should drive spawn checks, world time, cap, or requests.",
